scenario power-up with the network off and a 2 h old cache: no clock, so protective (TP7)
# The board has no battery-backed clock. With no hotspot there is neither
# SNTP nor a server's Date header, so the cache's age is unknown: C = 1 and
# the operator LED blinks amber. TP7's "cache used" cannot pass after a power
# cycle with the network off unless an RTC is added; 24 and 29 show when it can.
net down
cache fresh
boot
wait 4.9
expect budget_set == 0         # still inside the 5 s cap
within 9 state == DARK_IDLE
expect clock == 0
expect source == PROTECTIVE
expect why == age-unknown
expect sky_c == 1
